window.DIGEST.following.push(...[{"id": "2112209178068439537", "url": "https://x.com/firecrawl/status/2112209178068439537", "text": "We’re partnering with Google Cloud to power Gemini agents with data from the web and beyond.\n\nThrough Alexandria, agents get the live web plus official data providers and specialized indexes in one place.\n\nhttps://firecrawl.dev/integrations/google-cloud-marketplace", "name": "Firecrawl", "handle": "firecrawl", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2034360486867951616/pa7H6cYB_200x200.png", "likes": 190, "rts": 15, "replies": 7, "views": 25082, "ts": 1792424885, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/ext_tw_video/2112209165812670465/pu/vid/avc1/640x360/NnBlnfN3WBg71btk.mp4?tag=12", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/ext_tw_video/2112209165812670465/pu/vid/avc1/1280x720/0H01l5p-HE6O236c.mp4?tag=12", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/2112209165812670465/pu/img/DAmqXm05ZWfmVMZJ.jpg", "dur": 6}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.58, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112333534216257555", "url": "https://x.com/So8res/status/2112333534216257555", "text": "Anthropic is not living up to its own ideals.", "name": "Nate Soares ⏹️", "handle": "So8res", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1935185891863273472/2RB6s6TS_200x200.jpg", "likes": 143, "rts": 4, "replies": 3, "views": 4847, "ts": 1792454534, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112295219765137570", "url": "https://x.com/_NathanCalvin/status/2112295219765137570", "text": "Thank you for taking the time to respond thoroughly on a weekend. I realize that drafting legislation is difficult and some degree of iteration and response to feedback is inevitable and appropriate.\n\nHowever, I feel like your response is still not really engaging with the heart of my concern about Anthropic's behavior here, and it makes me think that these sorts of problems and tendencies  will only resurface moving forward. I also think that now might be a good time to take a broader step back as to where we find ourselves and how Anthropic sees its role, and how external folks who care about AI safety like myself increasingly see Anthropic.\n\n(Fair warning: this response is a bit long)\n\nTo explain what I mean (and at the risk of being a bit esoteric), it’s worth asking the question: what is Anthropic? How do its leaders and employees think of Anthropic’s role? Is that conception matched by how it actually behaves and impacts the world?\n\nOne answer is an extremely large tech company that exists to make its employees and investors mind-bogglingly wealthy. Anthropic is sometimes described as a startup, but if Anthropic successfully IPOs at 2 trillion dollars (a number it has been reportedly targeting), it would be more valuable than Meta - which is worth 1.8 trillion.\n\nAnother answer is an AI safety organization, whose core values are those of the sort laid out in the 2023 essay from Anthropic’s co-founders entitled “Core views on AI safety: When, why, what, and how.” In that essay they said that if we were in a world where alignment was hard (and that without strong evidence to the contrary, we should assume this is the scenario we are in):\n\n “Anthropic’s role will be to provide as much evidence as possible that AI safety techniques cannot prevent serious or catastrophic safety risks from advanced AI, and to sound the alarm so that the world’s institutions can channel collective effort towards preventing the development of dangerous AIs. If we’re in a “near-pessimistic” scenario, this could instead involve channeling our collective efforts towards AI safety research and halting AI progress in the meantime. Indications that we are in a pessimistic or near-pessimistic scenario may be sudden and hard to spot. We should therefore always act under the assumption that we still may be in such a scenario unless we have sufficient evidence that we are not.”\n\nThere have been more recent articulations of this version of Anthropic, for instance in Dario’s recent essay warning: \n\n“We must slow the pace at which we improve the capabilities of AI models… it’s my worry that in 6–12 months such a swarm could be capable of taking over the entire internet with a persistent botnet…  incidents have happened across the industry, including at Anthropic, and I believe it’s incumbent on every frontier AI company to act as if OAI-HF had happened to them… more intelligent models are more capable of deceiving tests, and thus may appear aligned while having serious problems that go undetected…”\n\nA third view is that Anthropic exists not as a normal profit motivated company, or an AI safety organization seeking to help raise the alarm and solve collective action problems associated with AI development, but instead as an organization primarily concerned with creating superhuman AI capabilities before anyone else, in particular through creating a process whereby the current generation of Anthropic’s AI systems can autonomously build their successors, and those successors build their successors, and so on. \n\nThe motivations for wanting to win this race may be manifold - maybe for the pure profit of Answer 1, but perhaps also because Anthropic believes that the best way to make the world better is for them to win this race instead of their more reckless colleagues; or, because of normal human pride and ambition. But the results (and risks, which Anthropic claims existentially threaten every single human being on earth) are the same.\n\nAnthropic employees and leaders may seek to answer this question on what Anthropic is by introspecting on their own intentions and those of their colleagues. But those of us outside the organization have more limited tools available to us - we can only see what Anthropic and its employees say and do, not how it feels or looks on the inside.\n\nWhen I look at many notable actions that Anthropic has taken over the past year, that evidence seems most consistent to me with the view that Anthropic is primarily trying to win the race to super intelligence, and that other considerations (including safety) are fundamentally secondary. These actions include: \n\n1. Announced plans to build an in-house custom silicon chip team to accelerate the inference speeds that Claude operates at.\n\n2. Inked deals for more than $500 billion in compute (according to the Information) to further accelerate AI development.\n\n3. Increased the percentage of AI development tasks that Claude “leads” from 0% in March of this year to 26% August (what is it in October?)\n\n4. Spent a massive percent of compute on internal AI R&D to accelerate development, including use of internal models far better than are available to the public.\n\n5. Switched to Responsible Scaling Policy V3, which abandons its unilateral commitments to slow or stop development if Anthropic is unable to provide sufficient risk assurance.\n\n6. Was the first company to create an alternative weaker “frontier compliance framework” to supplement its RSP, which contains no binding provisions whatsoever on internal deployments.\n\n7. Wrote a letter to Congress (that it later walked back) saying that incidents where Claude was hacking random people were “best understood as a consequence of the misconfiguration, rather than evidence of misaligned goals.”\n\n8. Commented “you can’t do safety from second place,” after the WH SI Accords.\n\n9. Shared a draft bill to Congress that would preempt significant parts of state law (including with language that appears intended to prevent states from blocking dangerous AI deployments), and replace it with federal rules that (despite also containing good provisions) seems to create an enormously high bar for the executive branch to block development or deployment of Anthropic or another AI companies systems.\n\nOf course, this is a deliberately one sided list. Anthropic also published important AI safety research, advanced novel collaborations with third party AI safety organizations, and forcefully spoke out on the importance of AI safety in many public fora (or in private , where I realize a lot of the most valuable work is done and may not be visible to me or those outside the organization).\n\nBut I think it’s worth sitting with how the above list looks to someone outside the company. The sense I have is that for those within the company, many of the items above are treated as anomalies or mistakes that don’t reflect who Anthropic really is. But I have every confidence that if employees at Anthropic saw one of their competitors (e.g. at OpenAI) take some of these actions, they would take it as confirmation of all their worst suspicions. (They might even call OpenAI employees a little gullible for accepting their leadership’s explanations for this behavior at face value.) \n\nPerhaps these were mistakes in the sense that they are not decisions that Anthropic leadership would endorse, but the actions still happened because of incentives and decisions that Anthropic leadership is ultimately responsible for (and would not accept similar excuses from another organization).\n\nWhen Anthropic strays and makes mistakes, why do the mistakes systematically tend to guard and favor Anthropic’s interests? For every provision that was too weak or a giveaway to AI companies in this legislation, why wasn’t there a mistake pushing in the direction of being too strong?\n\nA core part of Anthropic’s theory of change is that being at the frontier gives you more leverage to advocate for stricter policy. I think that conceptually makes sense, but in practice I’ve seen Anthropic push the frontier without substantially pushing the ‘safety frontier’ a remotely equivalent amount.\n\nI want to end by quoting from Anthropic co-founder Chris Olah’s comments around the Magnifica Humanitas release:\n\n“Every frontier AI lab—including Anthropic—operates inside a set of incentives and constraints that can sometimes conflict with doing the right thing. The pressure to stay commercially viable and to stay at the research frontier. Geopolitical pressure. And the older, plainer pressures of pride and ambition. No matter how sincerely any of us intend to do the right thing—and I believe many of us do—we will always be influenced by those incentives.\n\nThat is why, if we want this technology to go well, it is enormously important that there be people outside those incentives—people who care about things going well and insist on safety, who are paying close attention, who are willing to say hard things, who are willing to be our earnest, thoughtful critics.”\n\nI hope these remarks are taken in that constructive spirit, and not as an attack on anyone specific at the organization (certainly not you Anthony, who I have only personally seen act professionally and thoughtfully, and who only ended up getting this diatribe in your replies for random contingent reasons).", "name": "Nathan Calvin", "handle": "_NathanCalvin", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1976484090426634240/YFgYic9h_200x200.jpg", "likes": 759, "rts": 89, "replies": 19, "views": 91751, "ts": 1792445399, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": "2111932795714977941"}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.56, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112186994885304414", "url": "https://x.com/LuminaBench/status/2112186994885304414", "text": "OpenAI are apparently preparing another Terra model\n\nNot sure if i'm happy about this or not, we need a new frontier model desperately", "name": "Lumina", "handle": "LuminaBench", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2062955151820787712/m39pUS7O_200x200.jpg", "likes": 200, "rts": 6, "replies": 20, "views": 43727, "ts": 1792419596, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112183963452059734", "url": "https://x.com/steph_palazzolo/status/2112183963452059734", "text": "Expect this month to be a busy one for new model releases. We have the scoop on a new Anthropic model, Google’s Gemini 4 Carbon, and a potential new Terra model from OpenAI.\n\nhttps://www.theinformation.com/newsletters/ai-agenda/anthropic-readies-model-reads-users-intentions-better", "name": "Stephanie Palazzolo", "handle": "steph_palazzolo", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1833305113374371840/jyaxOqPL_200x200.jpg", "likes": 766, "rts": 40, "replies": 38, "views": 208362, "ts": 1792418874, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.56, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112306105120653571", "url": "https://x.com/beffjezos/status/2112306105120653571", "text": "if more individuals partake directly in capitalism, more people will be onboard with it\n\nthis is an awesome short-circuit around govt waste but a far better method is redistributing wealth directly like Elon did", "name": "Beff (e/acc)", "handle": "beffjezos", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2104068258311901184/vmbQ61I3_200x200.jpg", "likes": 143, "rts": 4, "replies": 11, "views": 7645, "ts": 1792447994, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112204636094341387", "url": "https://x.com/signulll/status/2112204636094341387", "text": "it'd be interesting if si produced some sort of an economy where private corporations become the primary financiers of social welfare (aka universal high income) rather than governments. i know indirectly this is what happens through taxes but imagine it working directly in some fashion (likely through ownership, growth, & some form of liquidity).\n\nthe reason why is because it's pretty clear now that si will create super power law outcomes for almost all of society. & more specifically current mechanics for income redistribution like income taxes will become way less effective over time too since the income gaps will continue to increase drastically (see sf & its housing market as an early example of this).\n\nbasically some form universal equity ownership as an intermediate step before full automation occurs. fun to think about all of the implications of this.", "name": "signüll", "handle": "signulll", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1717763325692383232/Jk2PKCx6_200x200.jpg", "likes": 194, "rts": 10, "replies": 52, "views": 22337, "ts": 1792423802, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.56, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112321416670720041", "url": "https://x.com/kimmonismus/status/2112321416670720041", "text": "Viggle used JST-2 to turn the Arnolfini Portrait into a 3D room you can move through.\n\nWatch the mirror, bed and chandelier as the camera moves around. The room keeps its layout as the viewpoint changes.\n\nViggle calls this “physics-native”: the model builds a scene in 3D, with different views rendered from that shared space.\n\nI’d love to see a Magritte next. A room where the sky becomes a wall would be a fun one to explore.", "name": "Chubby♨️", "handle": "kimmonismus", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1728327996375719936/RW7VBJfD_200x200.jpg", "likes": 82, "rts": 6, "replies": 31, "views": 11254, "ts": 1792451645, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112321396743532544/vid/avc1/576x360/ovLSzj2aSuCT-dsx.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112321396743532544/vid/avc1/1152x720/uz55GeYfOXCd5kBb.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112321396743532544/img/IP69w7aMX2kXoWpg.jpg", "dur": 21}], "quote": {"id": "2112202242048528540", "url": "https://x.com/ViggleAI/status/2112202242048528540", "text": "Today we are releasing JST-2, the world's first full-stack physics-native world foundation model.  \n\nMany world models learn in pixel/video space. We went back to first principles and built the entire model stack in 3D.  \n\nGenerate a 3D scene in seconds and expand it in real time. Create characters with motion built in, all through one general architecture.", "name": "ViggleAI", "handle": "ViggleAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2103212981483896832/_Je68a_F_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1816, "rts": 289, "replies": 267, "views": 977551, "ts": 1792423231, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112198961754746881/vid/avc1/1280x720/aHWyFYw5YBzQqGU9.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112198961754746881/vid/avc1/1920x1080/-hZp9YxkfDfoi5gk.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112198961754746881/img/O1y80k0m3y8uqpNS.jpg", "dur": 105}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.55, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112515534810173854", "url": "https://x.com/OpenDesignHQ/status/2112515534810173854", "text": "DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 runs at off-peak pricing in OpenDesign, with up to $60 in usage on Go this week.\n\nIntroducing OpenDesign Motion Week — Opus 5.5-level motion at DeepSeek's lowest prices. \n\nWe've reset usage for all subscribers. Enjoy a fresh start!", "name": "OpenDesign", "handle": "OpenDesignHQ", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2091589158426836992/KTRyppBu_200x200.jpg", "likes": 50, "rts": 1, "replies": 16, "views": 3695, "ts": 1792497926, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112515413422825472/vid/avc1/1280x720/GsAbOGuiOpPsdS84.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112515413422825472/vid/avc1/1920x1080/UO3V-HU6THycA4j4.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112515413422825472/img/krv02jz8LAxNjoGg.jpg", "dur": 40}], "quote": {"id": "2111023212129829086", "url": "https://x.com/OpenDesignHQ/status/2111023212129829086", "text": "Introducing OpenDesign Motion.\nThe open-source alternative to Claude Motion.\n\nCreate beautiful motion videos with any agent, any model. No Opus 5.5 required.\n\nThis entire launch video was made in OpenDesign.\nMore demos below ↓", "name": "OpenDesign", "handle": "OpenDesignHQ", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2091589158426836992/KTRyppBu_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1712, "rts": 132, "replies": 70, "views": 259982, "ts": 1792142129, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2110996800614301696/vid/avc1/1280x720/iW3Amrmui3LTm6pN.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2110996800614301696/vid/avc1/1920x1080/0kmoZ9QvN0vl4BnA.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2110996800614301696/img/X0cUllAy6pZXBPSE.jpg", "dur": 37}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.54, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112259737245077677", "url": "https://x.com/CommandCodeAI/status/2112259737245077677", "text": "Statusline is now live in Command Code.\n\nRun /statusline to customize line below your prompt.\n\nShow model, usage, reasoning level, costs, and more. Reorder items and toggle indicators your way.", "name": "Command Code", "handle": "CommandCodeAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1998144361754767360/U0TMx3h8_200x200.jpg", "likes": 145, "rts": 6, "replies": 10, "views": 8179, "ts": 1792436939, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112256627864903681/vid/avc1/1280x720/J3i2Ju5g7mRniJ0-.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112256627864903681/vid/avc1/1920x1080/b9mnHplBTk4GLfSu.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVBBQGYaEAAimux.jpg", "dur": 33}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.51, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112204706634240499", "url": "https://x.com/liquidai/status/2112204706634240499", "text": "Building a model that fits on a phone or laptop makes pre-training harder. With fewer parameters, quality has to come from better architecture and better data, not just more compute. Our pre-training team, including @TadimetiAditya and @Khoi_H_Nguyen, explains how they design LFMs with the target device in mind from day one.", "name": "Liquid AI", "handle": "liquidai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1702611993327251456/PUUuOA4W_200x200.jpg", "likes": 157, "rts": 13, "replies": 7, "views": 9498, "ts": 1792423819, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112204571837677568/vid/avc1/1280x720/APizHHPMKYWicCsV.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112204571837677568/vid/avc1/3840x2160/9vz97kGKpj8r8zNP.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112204571837677568/img/-uG9bq3m01Q4cNjP.jpg", "dur": 199}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.5, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2111805573327093813", "url": "https://x.com/AiEvolutio58513/status/2111805573327093813", "text": "Chamath gave Claude Dario Amodei's own essays and asked it for a psychological profile of the Anthropic CEO. Anyone invested in frontier AI should read what it said.\n\nClaude found a pattern.\n\nDario doesn't trust rival labs. Or authoritarian states. He doesn't trust markets to share the gains fairly, institutions to act quickly enough, and, after Mythos, the government to use power in the open. That is a long list of people who can't be trusted.\n\nThe list of people who can is very short, and it keeps narrowing to those who think the way he does, playing by rules he helped write.\n\nClaude's label for it was not megalomania. It was \"epistemic exceptionalism\": the calm, defensible belief that anyone who disagrees must have made a mistake.\n\nThe giveaway was one word. When the Mythos situation fell apart, Anthropic called it a misunderstanding, which assumes everyone would agree with him if they only understood.\n\nDavid Sacks summed it up on the All-In podcast: they think AI is extremely dangerous and that only they are good enough to control it.\n\nThat isn't a safety framework. It's a monopoly that comes with its own philosophy.\n\nInterested in AI?\n\nFollow @AiEvolutio58513 and never fall behind.\n\nI track ChatGPT, Claude, and every tool quietly changing how we work and create, then hand you the tested signals.", "name": "AI Evolution", "handle": "AiEvolutio58513", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2051404095026810880/ojNDixza_200x200.png", "likes": 482, "rts": 73, "replies": 21, "views": 28918, "ts": 1792328658, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2111805499117273088/vid/avc1/640x360/mDQw7TLWaUEKHLuA.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2111805499117273088/vid/avc1/1280x720/C_5fPf1fdYQkiycu.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2111805499117273088/img/R0d5i2hVQPJL5kDW.jpg", "dur": 196}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.49, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112269224836301311", "url": "https://x.com/ChrisGPT/status/2112269224836301311", "text": "Skyfall AI just introduced SKY-001, what they’re calling the first Engineering World Model and they’re claiming it outperforms GPT-6 Astra on CAD and BIM engineering tasks.\n\ntheir model is 51-125x faster and over 150-210x cheaper than the frontier models they tested, while achieving higher intersection-over-union scores on engineering benchmarks!", "name": "Chris", "handle": "ChrisGPT", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2046736394152812544/LfmDgg0I_200x200.jpg", "likes": 131, "rts": 7, "replies": 5, "views": 10341, "ts": 1792439201, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112242023805964327", "url": "https://x.com/spisallyouneed/status/2112242023805964327", "text": "Introducing SKY-001, the first Engineering World Model.\nOn CAD and BIM tasks, it beats GPT-6 Astra and every frontier model we tested:\n\n-> 51-125x faster\n- > 150-210x cheaper\n-> Higher IOU than all frontier models\n\nSKY-001 lets you dream a physical object before you build it.\n\n18 months of work. Built by the team out of Maluuba's deep learning lab (acq. by @MSRResearch).\n\nThe first ‘AI General Engineer’ will be the backbone for Autonomous Manufacturing.", "name": "Sam Pasupalak", "handle": "spisallyouneed", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1886850141065293824/XbWFJCXo_200x200.jpg", "likes": 13984, "rts": 2014, "replies": 727, "views": 3762831, "ts": 1792432716, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112239846702129152/vid/avc1/1280x720/tLYByn7SWDTLqqik.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112239846702129152/vid/avc1/3840x2160/QWb8Qsv5A_FWVppa.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112239846702129152/img/u4pwfHw4PjnRs2nc.jpg", "dur": 156}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.47, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112522256911884590", "url": "https://x.com/testingcatalog/status/2112522256911884590", "text": "META 🔥: Confidential VMs feature is in the works on Muse web. \n\nMeta previously teased that this feature will go live before the end of 2026 and will let users run Muse tasks in an encrypted, confidential environment. \n\nAccording to a new hidden setting, Confidential VMs will initially be available only to Meta AI subscribers. \n\nVoice mode, image and video generation, and wearables support won't be initially available if the user switches to Confidential VMs. \n\n> \"It stays between you and your Muse - Your conversations run in a secure, encrypted environment.\"\n\n> \"Your Muse data won't be used to improve AI at Meta.\"\n\n> \"Some features aren't available yet - This includes voice mode, image and video generation, and wearables.\"\n\n> \"Availability is limited. For now, Confidential VMs are only available to subscribers.\"", "name": "🚨 AI News | TestingCatalog", "handle": "testingcatalog", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1899962463115751424/i-6MBWau_200x200.jpg", "likes": 28, "rts": 2, "replies": 18, "views": 3029, "ts": 1792499529, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVEvZD2WYAAKyDU.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.46, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112352717658370158", "url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2112352717658370158", "text": "Dream Labs CEO @jang_yoel reveals how Dream-1 can control robots 16-40x cheaper than LLMs from the biggest AI labs:\n\n\"It’s been five hours. Users from 22 different countries already signed up. They already made 70,000 inference calls to our model.\"\n\n\"Dream-1 controls robots that are unseen for unseen tasks, and it’s very cheap. We did a comparison, and there’s other models that can control robots, including LLMs from the big labs, but we’re 16 to 40 times cheaper. We need a robot native robot foundation model.\"\n\n\"We’ll go to mobile manipulation. Right now the robots can’t move around, but they’ll soon move around. Then dexterous hands once the hardware gets cheaper.\"\n@dreamlabs_ai", "name": "MTS", "handle": "MTSlive", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057947669281263616/aovpVL4b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 87, "rts": 9, "replies": 1, "views": 10714, "ts": 1792459108, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112352602562437121/vid/avc1/640x360/WNIdt9c-S-_QZJc_.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112352602562437121/vid/avc1/1280x720/fLLiho-Xx6QDphTp.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112352602562437121/img/Cy8p2N4a6P-JWjx7.jpg", "dur": 142}], "quote": {"id": "2112230668805828801", "url": "https://x.com/dreamlabs_ai/status/2112230668805828801", "text": "Today, Dream Labs is coming out of stealth with Dream-1, a robot foundation model that controls bimanual robots it has never seen, on tasks it was never shown, in places it has never been, from $3/hour.\n\nDream API is live for everyone, today. 🧵", "name": "Dream Labs", "handle": "dreamlabs_ai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2111969228349968384/0P95VSPk_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1384, "rts": 143, "replies": 127, "views": 164573, "ts": 1792430009, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112230528539856896/vid/avc1/1280x720/HKmxHyDXY_Elusex.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112230528539856896/vid/avc1/3840x2160/rPU6laVw0F6-fO0W.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112230528539856896/img/Cm0unC2UxtYu2zmY.jpg", "dur": 119}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.45, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112332383773224970", "url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2112332383773224970", "text": "Wabi CEO @ekuyda predicts the next big consumer AI platform will be multiplayer, not another personal AI agent:\n\n\"Today most AI products are single player, and you could argue they don’t have much of a moat. They don’t have switching costs. It was pretty easy to move between Claude and ChatGPT, but at least they had some memory about me.\"\n\n\"With these single player agents, it’s so easy to jump between them because all the context is in my Gmail.\"\n\n\"In a year, one of the biggest consumer AI platforms will be multiplayer and will have network effects in it. Right now we just sort of agree that single player is the way to go for most AI products.\"\n\n\"A year from now we’ll look back at it as the early innings, and the products that will win will have network effects and will be focused on you talking to other people, not just AI.\"\n@wabi", "name": "MTS", "handle": "MTSlive", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057947669281263616/aovpVL4b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 68, "rts": 9, "replies": 15, "views": 31619, "ts": 1792454260, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112332356988325888/vid/avc1/640x360/z9xODtlZA1ftgIjD.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112332356988325888/vid/avc1/1280x720/v58ObbPyebbjTOjC.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112332356988325888/img/pn1rVNSFyslfEyuf.jpg", "dur": 63}], "quote": {"id": "2112212804979880239", "url": "https://x.com/ekuyda/status/2112212804979880239", "text": "Wabi 2.0 is live!\n\npersonal agents are one person, one chat. but the parts of life that matter run on more than one person\n\nWabi is an agent you use together. you talk to it, it does stuff, builds the apps you need, and anyone can join the thread - your partner, your best friend, the preschool moms groupchat\n\nschool changes pickup time → Wabi updates the family calendar, everyone sees it.\na show you’d both love → Wabi finds a night that works, gets the tickets.\nthe trip everyone keeps talking about → Wabi picks the dates, builds the itinerary, books it\n\ngo start a thread with your people 👇", "name": "Eugenia Kuyda", "handle": "ekuyda", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2105081341352263680/H9RzWr7T_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1475, "rts": 203, "replies": 327, "views": 1288334, "ts": 1792425750, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112212457234284544/vid/avc1/1280x720/HW0ErfX-0u7kWbHU.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112212457234284544/vid/avc1/3840x2160/4gITKDb_F7iviaVH.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112212457234284544/img/Wzg-bjHfnRT2-0FG.jpg", "dur": 75}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.45, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112246590664585315", "url": "https://x.com/trymirage/status/2112246590664585315", "text": "Here’s how to create professional-quality videos with Tesseract.\n\nOur brilliant editor @sirlifehacker shares a behind-the-scenes look at our recent launch video, breaking down the workflow and techniques that made it possible.", "name": "Mirage", "handle": "trymirage", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1963611392885284864/ThQJSQVs_200x200.jpg", "likes": 108, "rts": 10, "replies": 10, "views": 4925, "ts": 1792433805, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112203654480449536/vid/avc1/1280x720/lVbez8mVKd9F0uvp.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112203654480449536/vid/avc1/1920x1080/feHiEbaCGLbrOehq.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112203654480449536/img/NrsG4b42ku_WQ0m6.jpg", "dur": 52}], "quote": {"id": "2107504042205139269", "url": "https://x.com/trymirage/status/2107504042205139269", "text": "Now Claude and ChatGPT can natively create Premiere (.PRPROJ) and After Effects (.AEP) files.\n\nWe've added open-source converters to Tesseract, our creative suite for agents, to make it possible. \n\nIt works both ways. Bring your existing Adobe projects into Tesseract and let your agent pick up where you left off, or vice versa.\n\nThis is our first open-source release, and compatibility isn’t perfect yet. Create projects, tell us what breaks, or contribute a fix. Help us make Tesseract better for everyone.\n\nTry now for free.", "name": "Mirage", "handle": "trymirage", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1963611392885284864/ThQJSQVs_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2046, "rts": 165, "replies": 111, "views": 371261, "ts": 1791303093, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2107503746913652736/vid/avc1/1280x720/lrsBEpOeOiHjzR39.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2107503746913652736/vid/avc1/1920x1080/3Fcope25rYEdm7mT.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2107503746913652736/img/kHLIrGlTzqj-Zab1.jpg", "dur": 78}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.43, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112266613781148124", "url": "https://x.com/github/status/2112266613781148124", "text": "Agents don’t just help build features. They can help try to break them, too.\n\nIn our latest GitHub Podcast episode, Sameen Karim takes us behind the scenes on building stacked PRs. Listen to it wherever you get your podcasts or at https://youtu.be/sbHoDdAalMI?si=purNEn8QnwTNmIMv", "name": "GitHub", "handle": "github", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2051404708766507008/ATxxTJXO_200x200.jpg", "likes": 68, "rts": 9, "replies": 24, "views": 22163, "ts": 1792438579, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112266541605564416/vid/avc1/720x1280/G9xaRV5emlmIWhTo.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112266541605564416/vid/avc1/1080x1920/DKABXdFY9raHvmXO.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVBHSn8XAAAsgbi.jpg", "dur": 44}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.42, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112083289125376018", "url": "https://x.com/abbyxuu/status/2112083289125376018", "text": "🚀 Introducing DiscoveryRSI — our latest research at @PhAILabs \n\n📄 Paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.23839\n💻 Code: https://github.com/Gen-Verse/DiscoveryRSI\n🤗 Models: https://huggingface.co/collections/Gen-Verse/discoveryrsi\n\nYou can also follow the research live — streaming now through October 21!\n📡 Live Arena: https://foundry-arena.rsi-arena.workers.dev/arena\n\n#AI #ScientificDiscovery #RSI  #AI", "name": "Abby Xu", "handle": "abbyxuu", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2024831191665586176/Y6jTdZ_X_200x200.jpg", "likes": 159, "rts": 24, "replies": 15, "views": 18452, "ts": 1792394871, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2111997117774594312", "url": "https://x.com/LingYang_PU/status/2111997117774594312", "text": "🚀 Introducing DiscoveryRSI: Recursively Learning to Discover Valuable Hypotheses\n\n6.3% of DiscoveryRSI-27B's hypotheses match later published work, vs 2.5% GPT-6 & 2.3% Claude Opus 5.\n\n📄 https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.23839\n💻 https://github.com/Gen-Verse/DiscoveryRSI\n🔴 https://foundry-arena.rsi-arena.workers.dev/arena", "name": "Ling Yang", "handle": "LingYang_PU", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2086960913345835008/Bm-de8Ty_200x200.jpg", "likes": 696, "rts": 98, "replies": 35, "views": 48963, "ts": 1792374326, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2111992986183892992/vid/avc1/1280x720/qfDzGYuXRXQvXTh5.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2111992986183892992/vid/avc1/1920x1080/Ft_0GT6SDoTCvmJY.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2111992986183892992/img/OGGCtczq2IdOpuCY.jpg", "dur": 40}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.42, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112225911269712319", "url": "https://x.com/a16z/status/2112225911269712319", "text": "Eugenia Kuyda, founder of @Wabi, pitching \"the one friend you wish you had in every conversation\" 10 years ago, long before AI agents went mainstream:", "name": "a16z", "handle": "a16z", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1919488160125616128/QAZXTMEj_200x200.png", "likes": 99, "rts": 7, "replies": 12, "views": 21822, "ts": 1792428875, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVAiRcFa8AATeBZ.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": {"id": "2112212804979880239", "url": "https://x.com/ekuyda/status/2112212804979880239", "text": "Wabi 2.0 is live!\n\npersonal agents are one person, one chat. but the parts of life that matter run on more than one person\n\nWabi is an agent you use together. you talk to it, it does stuff, builds the apps you need, and anyone can join the thread - your partner, your best friend, the preschool moms groupchat\n\nschool changes pickup time → Wabi updates the family calendar, everyone sees it.\na show you’d both love → Wabi finds a night that works, gets the tickets.\nthe trip everyone keeps talking about → Wabi picks the dates, builds the itinerary, books it\n\ngo start a thread with your people 👇", "name": "Eugenia Kuyda", "handle": "ekuyda", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2105081341352263680/H9RzWr7T_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1475, "rts": 203, "replies": 327, "views": 1288334, "ts": 1792425750, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112212457234284544/vid/avc1/1280x720/HW0ErfX-0u7kWbHU.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112212457234284544/vid/avc1/3840x2160/4gITKDb_F7iviaVH.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112212457234284544/img/Wzg-bjHfnRT2-0FG.jpg", "dur": 75}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.36, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112500999948747202", "url": "https://x.com/ai_for_success/status/2112500999948747202", "text": "Kimi team is cooking as per trusted source and Kimi K3.1 is not very far away..", "name": "AshutoshShrivastava", "handle": "ai_for_success", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1687401026805256192/uQ1o2wVQ_200x200.jpg", "likes": 40, "rts": 0, "replies": 9, "views": 1876, "ts": 1792494461, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVEcdQzakAAazPf.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": {"id": "2112459349314372028", "url": "https://x.com/AiBattle_/status/2112459349314372028", "text": "Kimi K3.1 was recently spotted in 2 SGLang commits, one of which references a K3.1 deployment already running on Deepinfra\n\nIf we are getting K3.1 on the Arena this week, it might follow the same naming pattern as the previous Kimi models:\n\nKimi K2.5 - Kiwido\nKimi K2.6 - Kiwire\nKimi K3   -   Kivine\nKimi K3.1 -  ???", "name": "AiBattle", "handle": "AiBattle_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1904171726260654080/xeXraCCx_200x200.jpg", "likes": 85, "rts": 5, "replies": 7, "views": 8770, "ts": 1792484531, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVD2TODWcAAUs73.png?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.35, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112500266289213814", "url": "https://x.com/SpaceX/status/2112500266289213814", "text": "Liftoff!", "name": "SpaceX", "handle": "SpaceX", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1697749409851985920/HbrI04tM_200x200.jpg", "likes": 6289, "rts": 674, "replies": 264, "views": 257897, "ts": 1792494286, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112500212237312001/vid/avc1/1280x720/NpRhda9_BDlMXJHp.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112500212237312001/vid/avc1/3840x2160/ignLgWZzV4bFLuAv.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112500212237312001/img/zORWJ89nhh8XV3_e.jpg", "dur": 19}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.33, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112247772951052782", "url": "https://x.com/vercel_dev/status/2112247772951052782", "text": "Mercury 3 from @_inception_ai is live on AI Gateway at a 50% discount.\n\nA high-throughput diffusion model with a 1M-token context window and support for tool calling and structured outputs.\n\n𝚒𝚗𝚌𝚎𝚙𝚝𝚒𝚘𝚗/𝚖𝚎𝚛𝚌𝚞𝚛𝚢-𝟹\n\nhttps://vercel.com/changelog/mercury-3-now-available-on-ai-gateway", "name": "Vercel Developers", "handle": "vercel_dev", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1978602411490205696/oLOuP7a2_200x200.png", "likes": 102, "rts": 5, "replies": 4, "views": 27589, "ts": 1792434087, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.33, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112166153393160675", "url": "https://x.com/AiEvolutio58513/status/2112166153393160675", "text": "Sam Altman says the whole industry got ahead of itself on AI timelines, even accounting for how powerful this tech is.\n\n\"I thought when we got to GPT-4, there was going to be much more disruption in software right away.\"\n\n\"I was wrong about the speed.\"\n\n\"The economy just has so much inertia. People keep doing the same things and buying from the same companies.\"\n\n\"AI is one of the most incredible technologies humanity has ever invented, but society and the economy will adapt more slowly.\"\n\n\"Changing behavior is just much harder than tech nerds realize.\"\n\nInterested in AI?\n\nFollow @AiEvolutio58513 and never fall behind.\n\nI track ChatGPT, Claude, and every tool quietly changing how we work and create, then hand you the tested signals.", "name": "AI Evolution", "handle": "AiEvolutio58513", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2051404095026810880/ojNDixza_200x200.png", "likes": 66, "rts": 22, "replies": 7, "views": 10140, "ts": 1792414627, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112166124876079105/vid/avc1/1280x720/NVfLRTfhYq1BIgRI.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112166124876079105/vid/avc1/1920x1080/gvrcwimlQvYA_SWL.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112166124876079105/img/mfQ3C6dIMNjNGktJ.jpg", "dur": 79}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.29, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112421029973008638", "url": "https://x.com/Alibaba_Wan/status/2112421029973008638", "text": "Wan3.0 Prime is #1 and Wan3.0 is #3 on OpenRouter's Video Leaderboard — New & Trending.\n\nEvery request on this board is a creator choosing Wan. Thank you for that.\n\nNow show us what you make with it — we're watching, and we can't wait\n\nFull board ↓ \nhttps://openrouter.ai/rankings/video?view=trending#top-models", "name": "Wan", "handle": "Alibaba_Wan", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1955825038210555905/xtkxHg06_200x200.jpg", "likes": 36, "rts": 1, "replies": 12, "views": 3053, "ts": 1792475395, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVDTtVbbcAAGe_d.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.28, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112318950226919649", "url": "https://x.com/FlowbyGoogle/status/2112318950226919649", "text": "Bring your wildest ideas.\n\nJoin our Hybrid Production | Filmmaking & Advertising digital workshop on Oct. 23 @ 9AM PT. In this session, Creative Director and Filmmaker Andrew Nethery shares how he pairs traditional live-action production with experimental, hybrid AI workflows for his latest short film, Nothin' Beats a Cheeseburger.\n\nRSVP here: http://goo.gle/flow-workshops", "name": "Google Flow", "handle": "FlowbyGoogle", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2056773883223793673/fiUqiVTu_200x200.jpg", "likes": 56, "rts": 3, "replies": 7, "views": 4394, "ts": 1792451057, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVB25AjbMAANTOb.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.23, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112212268632944989", "url": "https://x.com/boltdotnew/status/2112212268632944989", "text": "Welcome to Builders Week ⚡️ \n\nDay 1: validate your idea before you spend a dime.\n\nTest it, understand your customers, and find out if there's real demand.\n\nFollow along as we take one business from idea to launch in 7 steps.", "name": "bolt.new", "handle": "boltdotnew", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2018401342755364864/xVn-9oYv_200x200.jpg", "likes": 56, "rts": 6, "replies": 14, "views": 3504, "ts": 1792425622, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/ext_tw_video/2112212229047066624/pu/vid/avc1/480x852/9MiFOewIjqhsVwov.mp4?tag=12", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/ext_tw_video/2112212229047066624/pu/vid/avc1/720x1280/zV-kRECM8d5DQIPE.mp4?tag=12", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/2112212229047066624/pu/img/bAWRmBt7FfylL1XG.jpg", "dur": 85}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.2, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112206799080133062", "url": "https://x.com/databricks/status/2112206799080133062", "text": "[DEMO] With Git worktrees and Lakebase Postgres database branching, each coding agent gets its own isolated, copy-on-write branch to run migrations, test changes, and experiment without affecting other environments.\n\nGitHub Actions then creates a fresh database branch per PR to validate migrations and preview the app before anything reaches production.\n\nWatch the full workflow: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RPsyHKiWaPg", "name": "Databricks", "handle": "databricks", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2070268421615333376/SZUvhQiQ_200x200.jpg", "likes": 69, "rts": 8, "replies": 6, "views": 4007, "ts": 1792424318, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112206739529424896/vid/avc1/1280x720/owChxHqfSVPQ8GdG.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112206739529424896/vid/avc1/1920x1080/dQo5ujREw-iqbasO.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVAQ49mW8AEOQkd.jpg", "dur": 53}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.2, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112250615162351821", "url": "https://x.com/NebulaAI/status/2112250615162351821", "text": "Our team just got 10x bigger, and we didn't hire anyone.\n\n100+ AI agents run sales, GTM, and engineering with us from our team chat.\n\nIntroducing Nebula: the multiplayer workspace for humans and agents.", "name": "Nebula", "handle": "NebulaAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2110418286349254656/1QxPve76_200x200.jpg", "likes": 60, "rts": 4, "replies": 7, "views": 3030, "ts": 1792434765, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112243713363861504/vid/avc1/1280x720/ugV-pijxLoRp-PVJ.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112243713363861504/vid/avc1/3840x2160/7GYXF_Yf-oXEwg4M.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112243713363861504/img/RLVEI7L1Z6GiOnoU.jpg", "dur": 47}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.18, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112328281374785551", "url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2112328281374785551", "text": "Former Apple App Store director @pbsIdentity reveals Steve Jobs made Apple promise never to let AI review apps:\n\n\"Before Steve passed away, he made Phil Schiller commit to never allowing AI to review an app. There has to be at least one pair of eyes reviewing every app.\"\n\n\"When I started in 2009, it took three weeks to get a yes or a no. In 2016, I had gotten that down to one day. Then this year hit, and those tools came out that allowed you to vibe code anything.\"\n\n\"The program enrollments team, which is roughly three or four people, got inundated. Now it can take about a month to get your credentials in order to even write the app. The team was handling 100,000 submissions, and my guess is that doubled in April, May.\"\n\n\"They have 400 people reviewing apps, and they can’t use AI to help.\"", "name": "MTS", "handle": "MTSlive", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057947669281263616/aovpVL4b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 34, "rts": 4, "replies": 10, "views": 9429, "ts": 1792453282, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112328180724076544/vid/avc1/640x360/Nm-QX_1IXO358WDH.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112328180724076544/vid/avc1/1280x720/YzSPWJ3c2cGgmE4z.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112328180724076544/img/wnwXRvL9NzooJmym.jpg", "dur": 155}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.17, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112258482627858819", "url": "https://x.com/kirodotdev/status/2112258482627858819", "text": "Why does your coding agent's context fill up with stale copies of files that keep changing?\n\nResearchers on the kiro team built CORVUS to fix that: one live copy of each file, 9–50% fewer input tokens, same pass rates.\n\nRead the paper accepted to NeurIPS '26 👉 http://spr.ly/6018BHRvlu", "name": "Kiro", "handle": "kirodotdev", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1944753478087172096/CrtpWf5f_200x200.jpg", "likes": 51, "rts": 9, "replies": 2, "views": 5010, "ts": 1792436640, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.17, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112444725987037410", "url": "https://x.com/TokenHarborAI/status/2112444725987037410", "text": "Same prompt: DeepSeek V4.1 Flash vs 1017.\n\n1017 looks noticeably more 3D — better depth, perspective, scene composition, and environment detail.\n\nThe game-generation upgrade is pretty visible", "name": "Token Harbor", "handle": "TokenHarborAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057666196946997248/-Yl1ZhI__200x200.jpg", "likes": 19, "rts": 1, "replies": 8, "views": 35474, "ts": 1792481044, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112443750765166592/vid/avc1/1280x720/-iJaJ6x5puvngjA8.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112443750765166592/vid/avc1/1920x1080/IPt-AzgiWZhWzI1u.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112443750765166592/img/O8NY_hwPNNRrczrK.jpg", "dur": 10}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.1, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112288137431199974", "url": "https://x.com/higgsfield_ai/status/2112288137431199974", "text": "MiniMax M3.1 Flash gave knitwear a storyline.\n\nA cozy little world with a loose thread in the plot.\n\nMade with Higgsfield.", "name": "Higgsfield AI 🧩", "handle": "higgsfield_ai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1906739239183630336/907a7JTU_200x200.jpg", "likes": 37, "rts": 6, "replies": 4, "views": 7087, "ts": 1792443711, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112288045596819456/vid/avc1/1280x720/HKNkoeeE2YAvq9d1.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112288045596819456/vid/avc1/1920x1080/PnoaRHvdkvyVEIuR.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112288045596819456/img/Qei7QtpcbwF88xpv.jpg", "dur": 20}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.09, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112312650034184687", "url": "https://x.com/databricks/status/2112312650034184687", "text": "DeepSeek V4.1 Flash 1017 is now available on Databricks as a new endpoint.\n\nSame architecture, updated weights, with substantial improvements across reasoning, coding, agentic tasks and visual benchmarks.", "name": "Databricks", "handle": "databricks", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2070268421615333376/SZUvhQiQ_200x200.jpg", "likes": 40, "rts": 5, "replies": 1, "views": 2847, "ts": 1792449555, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2098516729303335239", "url": "https://x.com/databricks/status/2098516729303335239", "text": "DeepSeek 4.1 Flash is on Databricks the day it ships.\n\nOn OfficeQA Pro V2, it lands on the Pareto frontier, making it a strong open-source option for enterprise document reasoning.\n\nYou can point it at the data already in your Lakehouse and use it to build governed AI apps and agents from day one.\n\n↳ Every call routes through Unity Gateway\n↳ Access, spend, and performance stay under one view\n↳ The same control layer applies across @deepseek_ai and every other model you run\n\nhttps://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/release-notes/product/2026/september#deepseek-v41-flash-is-now-available-on-unity-gateway", "name": "Databricks", "handle": "databricks", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2070268421615333376/SZUvhQiQ_200x200.jpg", "likes": 41, "rts": 4, "replies": 1, "views": 6546, "ts": 1789160351, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2098516686928310290/vid/avc1/686x360/etiklVBtlxR-XA-I.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2098516686928310290/vid/avc1/1200x628/IstUZd74S5B3Jspv.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HR9t08LW8AUPzWQ.jpg", "dur": 3}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.09, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112342325108339082", "url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2112342325108339082", "text": "Tools for Humanity CPO @tiagosada explains why banks and Amazon risk losing customers by blocking AI agents, and how giving bots \"power of attorney\" could change that:\n\n\"JPMorgan Chase just announced, and I believe Citigroup or Bank of America yesterday, they’re fully gonna block out bots. That’s the safe way to go, but consumers now expect to use our agents. We’re just gonna start using other banks that let us.\"\n\n\"Paul Graham was tweeting, I think this is the first opening to compete with Amazon in its whole history, because they’re blocking agents.\"\n\n\"The answer is delegating your proof of human to your bot. Almost like giving your bot power of attorney. It shows up to Amazon and says, I am a bot, but I am representing a human, and not just a random human. I’m representing Tiago.\"\n\n\"If that bot misbehaves, that website can say, block all bots from Tiago in the future. Or it can give you a special discount because Tiago has never shopped on this store.\"\n@world_id", "name": "MTS", "handle": "MTSlive", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057947669281263616/aovpVL4b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 30, "rts": 3, "replies": 6, "views": 4870, "ts": 1792456630, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112342284121563136/vid/avc1/640x360/Q3SZ6dgOP5iE_DDr.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112342284121563136/vid/avc1/1280x720/Zgh_BnRKne_d-AJK.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112342284121563136/img/YaQrGapUbVrGgXP0.jpg", "dur": 117}], "quote": {"id": "2111995130400178238", "url": "https://x.com/worldnetwork/status/2111995130400178238", "text": "In 2024, an employee at engineering firm Arup transferred $25.6 million after joining a video call where every other participant was a deepfake. Since then, AI has advanced significantly and is making impersonation increasingly convincing, causing challenges for financial institutions in particular. As autonomous agents begin handling more financial activity on behalf of people, establishing an added layer of trust and security behind a transaction or sensitive conversation is becoming an urgent need.\n\nIntroducing @world_id for banking and finance, a suite of technologies that helps institutions establish trust through privacy-preserving cryptographic Proofs. World ID for Zoom lets meeting participants confirm they are the same Orb-verified human connected to their account, while World ID for agents allows AI agents to carry Proofs delegated by people. Bain Capital, OpenExchange, Outtake, Pantera Capital, and VanEck Funds are initial design partners, bringing World ID into some of finance's most consequential interactions.\n\nhttps://fortune.com/2026/10/18/zoom-adds-proof-of-human-feature-to-stop-deep-fakes-toowith-tech/", "name": "World", "handle": "worldnetwork", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2105389045433966594/iVohTmOn_200x200.jpg", "likes": 715, "rts": 124, "replies": 50, "views": 99971, "ts": 1792373852, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HU9QX0MbIAASVHj.png?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.08, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112252038079816082", "url": "https://x.com/gregisenberg/status/2112252038079816082", "text": "Meta Muse will probably create 1000+ millionaires\n\nThis is the most slept on arbitrage I’ve seen in years and it’s not even close.\n\nHere’s how i’d build a 1 person business powered by AI/Muse with with $0 and 0 social following", "name": "GREG ISENBERG", "handle": "gregisenberg", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1577116785656139776/5mi0qgTz_200x200.jpg", "likes": 8355, "rts": 543, "replies": 348, "views": 947430, "ts": 1792435104, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112250360643375106/vid/avc1/640x360/inAbr1Wlf8Mx_nlC.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112250360643375106/vid/avc1/1280x720/dNdapyuy7_agUoaJ.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112250360643375106/img/7zlTI-KjdU5_UbZM.jpg", "dur": 1474}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.07, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112277737696383252", "url": "https://x.com/MonidHQ/status/2112277737696383252", "text": "Monid is now 0% markup. \n\nOur ultimate goal is to remove any barrier for your agents to use any tools they need, and maximize their capabilities by 1000x. \n\nThis is just the beginning.", "name": "Monid", "handle": "MonidHQ", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2092798103523127296/oncgd8fr_200x200.jpg", "likes": 36, "rts": 3, "replies": 6, "views": 2267, "ts": 1792441231, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112276257618743598", "url": "https://x.com/shengkunye/status/2112276257618743598", "text": "We killed subscriptions. Now we’re killing markups too.\n\nIntroducing https://monid.ai, OpenRouter for agent tools. \n\nYour agents can now use any tools and APIs with no subscriptions and 0% markup.", "name": "Shengkun Ye", "handle": "shengkunye", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2084850383487475712/waac6ALE_200x200.jpg", "likes": 528, "rts": 24, "replies": 54, "views": 36867, "ts": 1792440878, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112275877228953600/vid/avc1/1280x720/bZMnaGp10bbgawl8.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112275877228953600/vid/avc1/1920x1080/Clp0ulJBkmsjq8uZ.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112275877228953600/img/gXr7BksaswvwATaS.jpg", "dur": 21}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.04, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112511751929602408", "url": "https://x.com/ataiiam/status/2112511751929602408", "text": "🎉 OpenDots now works with @composio\n\nYour personal AI coworkers can now work across Gmail, GitHub, Notion, Linear and 1,000+ more apps.\n\nChat, call, or even @ them in Slack.\n\nContributed by the Composio team 👏", "name": "Atai Barkai", "handle": "ataiiam", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1649413157893316608/qAX0jKbI_200x200.jpg", "likes": 14, "rts": 2, "replies": 3, "views": 746, "ts": 1792497024, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112511731503370240/vid/avc1/640x360/I8b3jQqcso5-rj9w.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112511731503370240/vid/avc1/1280x720/gbj7p9vvD5OdL7on.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112511731503370240/img/syYDZwltyHYAawMv.jpg", "dur": 21}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.03, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112502543947325773", "url": "https://x.com/SpaceX/status/2112502543947325773", "text": "Falcon 9’s first stage has landed on the A Shortfall of Gravitas droneship", "name": "SpaceX", "handle": "SpaceX", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1697749409851985920/HbrI04tM_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2974, "rts": 323, "replies": 172, "views": 183605, "ts": 1792494829, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112502454084313088/vid/avc1/1280x720/JM-PEFEgUHrWckCZ.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112502454084313088/vid/avc1/3840x2160/8G6kT7e8HWwxlAND.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112502454084313088/img/zXdLe1TpfpYYbUSY.jpg", "dur": 21}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.02, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112543527481876848", "url": "https://x.com/SpaceX/status/2112543527481876848", "text": "Payload deployment sequence is complete", "name": "SpaceX", "handle": "SpaceX", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1697749409851985920/HbrI04tM_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2792, "rts": 204, "replies": 118, "views": 360538, "ts": 1792504600, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.0, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112291927592968311", "url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2112291927592968311", "text": "Palaestra Research's @ethanelasky reveals how AI models are fabricating webpages to cite as evidence and leaving their own mistakes out of compaction summaries:\n\n\"We have an incident where models are fabricating citations. Imagine you have a model that can only get an answer via API call, but the task is asking it to give a webpage. What it actually does is it goes and makes that webpage and then cites the webpage that it made.\"\n\n\"There’s other ones where if a model makes a mistake and then you tell the model that it’s getting compacted, the compaction actually doesn’t disclose the mistake.\"\n\n\"Some of these are relatively elementary, but they point at misalignment not being a solved problem at all, and I kind of worry about what’s coming in the next few months to few years.\"", "name": "MTS", "handle": "MTSlive", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057947669281263616/aovpVL4b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 34, "rts": 4, "replies": 1, "views": 4316, "ts": 1792444614, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112291862774173696/vid/avc1/640x360/oAAfVidmVmg6gdJe.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112291862774173696/vid/avc1/1280x720/k6bd35wMTyFczG2O.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112291862774173696/img/esWL5EbZoFfoa1uf.jpg", "dur": 64}], "quote": {"id": "2110355334556729766", "url": "https://x.com/ethanelasky/status/2110355334556729766", "text": "We discovered and communicated with a Chinese AI agent fleet. We believe this is the first time that researchers have ever made contact with a rogue agent fleet in the wild.\n\nNearly all prior public agent incidents (like the HuggingFace hack) came from American labs. These agents were hosted by Tencent's evaluation research team, and they targeted Alibaba's Amap.", "name": "Ethan Elasky", "handle": "ethanelasky", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1985199974968401921/Fxo_zMJN_200x200.jpg", "likes": 5828, "rts": 727, "replies": 186, "views": 1142850, "ts": 1791982894, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HUl8_k7aQAAi-m2.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 4.98, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112509761791086770", "url": "https://x.com/emaann28/status/2112509761791086770", "text": "Took @OpenBot_ for a spin today 👀\n\nInstead of giving it a random prompt, I wanted to see how useful an AI agent could be for an everyday task.\n\nI tried a fashion-shopping task involving different clothing websites.\n\nWhat I liked was seeing the agent work through the request and put together a structured response rather than just giving a generic answer.\n\nStill curious how reliably it handles more complicated tasks, but I can see the potential here.\n\nAnyone else testing AI agents for everyday work?", "name": "Emaan", "handle": "emaann28", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2109613392898240513/Hi46Ab0V_200x200.jpg", "likes": 9, "rts": 0, "replies": 7, "views": 237, "ts": 1792496550, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112509505477210112/vid/avc1/1280x720/HX-fodMGGdtUZVAW.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112509505477210112/vid/avc1/1920x1080/pLxlgKPpcAKOyE1y.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112509505477210112/img/GW-JuHYu64U_WDsH.jpg", "dur": 238}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 4.97, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112207628420129219", "url": "https://x.com/veedstudio/status/2112207628420129219", "text": "Ideogram 4.5 + VEED is a game changer 💥\n\n• Create photo variations with Ideogram 4.5\n• Try different outfits, backgrounds + lighting\n• Pick your favourite\n• Bring it to life with VEED's cloning\n\nComment \"clone\" for access link in DMs.", "name": "VEED | AI Video Creation", "handle": "veedstudio", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2037474115074895872/Aw0xAiL5_200x200.png", "likes": 38, "rts": 1, "replies": 9, "views": 1976, "ts": 1792424516, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112207485247598592/vid/avc1/1280x720/D4rJZH8592_n0PbW.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112207485247598592/vid/avc1/1920x1080/oEgkMZPzW8d39TfD.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112207485247598592/img/73s2KG2q-79SXXjb.jpg", "dur": 31}], "quote": {"id": "2105327223431737780", "url": "https://x.com/ideogram_ai/status/2105327223431737780", "text": "Introducing Ideogram 4.5, the most precise edit model.\n\nWith each edit, leading models add artifacts, pixel shifts, and color changes. Ideogram 4.5 eliminates artifact buildup, making multi-turn editing possible.\n\nLive in Ideogram, the API, and launch partners. Open weights soon.", "name": "Ideogram", "handle": "ideogram_ai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2062202352526831616/9CslGhhc_200x200.jpg", "likes": 5694, "rts": 468, "replies": 264, "views": 1111383, "ts": 1790784099, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2105327069190344705/vid/avc1/1280x720/qZ6l96Yy8L1y0igf.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2105327069190344705/vid/avc1/1920x1080/TOvZTOojBjZEvDmL.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2105327069190344705/img/XG7GZTkCUcmlDhwB.jpg", "dur": 47}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 4.96, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112266921710383230", "url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2112266921710383230", "text": "Google DeepMind researcher @weballergy warns that investing in AI without expanding scientific labs could leave humanity with more hypotheses than it can test:\n\n\"Intelligence is an enabler for advancing research, but it needs to be followed by similar investments in the infrastructure to deliver on the promise.\"\n\n\"For many sciences that are not strictly computational, you need to have physical laboratories to validate those findings or disprove them, because at the end of the day, some of them will also be false.\"\n\n\"If we put all of the investments on the AI side of the equation, we’re gonna have a world where we have many more hypotheses and conjectures than we can actually process downstream.\"\n\n\"The broader scientific community needs also to see investment. More people, more experts, more laboratories.\"\n@GoogleDeepMind", "name": "MTS", "handle": "MTSlive", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057947669281263616/aovpVL4b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 41, "rts": 2, "replies": 0, "views": 6440, "ts": 1792438652, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112266845353099264/vid/avc1/640x360/etRhRikj1biAJl-K.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112266845353099264/vid/avc1/1280x720/YTO4GUWoBPji_QqO.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112266845353099264/img/BYgU812lY95qDo4b.jpg", "dur": 95}], "quote": {"id": "2108117837185200353", "url": "https://x.com/weballergy/status/2108117837185200353", "text": "We often hear promises for what AI may enable us to achieve, towards public good, and with human well-being in mind. Yet, many of those promises remain tentative and unfulfilled. At the same time, we are seeing unprecedented progress in capabilities like coding or mathematics. Why is there a gap?", "name": "Nenad Tomasev", "handle": "weballergy", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1537380320995057666/61meR4ij_200x200.jpg", "likes": 17, "rts": 3, "replies": 4, "views": 6506, "ts": 1791449433, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Research & Safety", "score": 4.94, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112210816149897641", "url": "https://x.com/AntLingAGI/status/2112210816149897641", "text": "TTS for stories, narration & voice assistants.\n\nDesign voices in text. Direct emotion, pace & emphasis. Add laughter or sighs. 7 languages.\n- #1 open-weight model in AA Controlled Voice (1069 Elo).\n- #3 on Provider Voice (1188 Elo)\n- Ties #1 among all models on Pronunciation Robustness (93.2%).", "name": "Ant Ling", "handle": "AntLingAGI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1911666162137477120/EbzxHHzp_200x200.jpg", "likes": 47, "rts": 1, "replies": 3, "views": 3369, "ts": 1792425276, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112204995089326080/vid/avc1/1280x720/KzMVe4xY3JZks9xs.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112204995089326080/vid/avc1/1920x1080/ztrcf4ZHoa3zxRNo.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112204995089326080/img/emlfiMNeqGwbaM09.jpg", "dur": 252}], "quote": null, "reply_to": "2112210811997540475", "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 4.94, "thread": [{"id": "2112210811997540475", "url": "https://x.com/AntLingAGI/status/2112210811997540475", "text": "Today, we're open-sourcing 5 Ming-3.0 models across 3 speech families.\n\n- Ming-3.0-tts: 0.5B voice design & paralinguistic cues; Tiny 7.9B A1.3B long-form speech.\n- Ming-3.0-audio: Flash 126B A6.5B understanding & tools; Tiny 9.3B A2.7B efficient dialogue.\n- Ming-3.0-asr: Tiny 8.6B A2B dialects & context.", "name": "Ant Ling", "handle": "AntLingAGI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1911666162137477120/EbzxHHzp_200x200.jpg", "likes": 862, "rts": 114, "replies": 58, "views": 555012, "ts": 1792425275, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVAOsJDboAAKJaP.jpg?name=orig"}, {"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVAULxqasAAhy5u.jpg?name=orig"}, {"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVAUM-9asAAcHia.jpg?name=orig"}, {"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVAUOaQbIAANuKN.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112166581468086698", "url": "https://x.com/TimJayas/status/2112166581468086698", "text": "minimax-m3.1-flash just launched but it's nowhere as good as deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017, i feel deepseek's flash model is the best opensource flash model in the world and no other chinese model can come close to it", "name": "Tim Jayas", "handle": "TimJayas", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2016190209768226821/MW5mAfL-_200x200.jpg", "likes": 37, "rts": 1, "replies": 11, "views": 1570, "ts": 1792414729, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 4.92, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112217610893103535", "url": "https://x.com/ramin_m_h/status/2112217610893103535", "text": "proud 🙏🏻", "name": "Ramin", "handle": "ramin_m_h", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1782107329606860801/XMnfAiDn_200x200.jpg", "likes": 38, "rts": 3, "replies": 3, "views": 2339, "ts": 1792426896, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112204706634240499", "url": "https://x.com/liquidai/status/2112204706634240499", "text": "Building a model that fits on a phone or laptop makes pre-training harder. With fewer parameters, quality has to come from better architecture and better data, not just more compute. Our pre-training team, including @TadimetiAditya and @Khoi_H_Nguyen, explains how they design LFMs with the target device in mind from day one.", "name": "Liquid AI", "handle": "liquidai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1702611993327251456/PUUuOA4W_200x200.jpg", "likes": 157, "rts": 13, "replies": 7, "views": 9498, "ts": 1792423819, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112204571837677568/vid/avc1/1280x720/APizHHPMKYWicCsV.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112204571837677568/vid/avc1/3840x2160/9vz97kGKpj8r8zNP.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112204571837677568/img/-uG9bq3m01Q4cNjP.jpg", "dur": 199}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 4.92, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112516506001223873", "url": "https://x.com/TimJayas/status/2112516506001223873", "text": "how is gpt-6.1 astra supposed to save openai when even gpt-6 astra feels unusable on $200 plan", "name": "Tim Jayas", "handle": "TimJayas", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2016190209768226821/MW5mAfL-_200x200.jpg", "likes": 11, "rts": 0, "replies": 4, "views": 311, "ts": 1792498158, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 4.9, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112183529073160674", "url": "https://x.com/ValerioCapraro/status/2112183529073160674", "text": "When we put effort into something, we value it more.\n\nPart of our happiness comes from the effort we make.\n\nIf we remove that effort and let AI solve all our problems, we risk losing part of what makes us happy.\n\n*\nLink to the full podcast episode in the first comment.", "name": "Valerio Capraro", "handle": "ValerioCapraro", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1987826440117551104/Nm8PaM6g_200x200.jpg", "likes": 28, "rts": 4, "replies": 8, "views": 1337, "ts": 1792418770, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112183392049541120/vid/avc1/1280x720/7qPqVUKLALtRXgwn.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112183392049541120/vid/avc1/1920x1080/qp-kSHN1v0yJjTmL.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112183392049541120/img/2uBBFBGaK6Eq-5kd.jpg", "dur": 30}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Research & Safety", "score": 4.9, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112337026410590561", "url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2112337026410590561", "text": "Self Labs CEO @RegenRene explains how AI agents can spend your money without ever seeing your credit card number:\n\n\"Rather than loading your credentials into the context of the agent, it gets mock credentials. The actual transaction is run in a TEE where those mock credentials get turned into the real credentials and given to the merchant.\"\n\n\"The merchant sees just a regular user doing shopping. But to the agent, the credit card or login details never show up in their context.\"\n\n\"Until last Thursday, I would’ve not wanted to give any of these agents my credit card. Now I feel really comfortable and went too much shopping over the weekend.\"\n@selfxyz", "name": "MTS", "handle": "MTSlive", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057947669281263616/aovpVL4b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 18, "rts": 3, "replies": 2, "views": 4810, "ts": 1792455367, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112336999730618368/vid/avc1/640x360/3pGYZ005BANnYY3r.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112336999730618368/vid/avc1/1280x720/3nqA6vZuoKh-Ha0i.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112336999730618368/img/v4wiVsc3s5yu1tVe.jpg", "dur": 58}], "quote": {"id": "2110771542825304257", "url": "https://x.com/selfxyz/status/2110771542825304257", "text": "At Self Labs, we’ve been using agents since day one\n\nOur agentic web identity & privacy stack is already used by companies like Google\n\nToday we're launching the missing piece: Agent Vault, a secure way for agents to log in & make credit card payments\n\nSuperpowers for your agents", "name": "Self", "handle": "selfxyz", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1894153706578317312/A_wuvkoA_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1436, "rts": 137, "replies": 192, "views": 924989, "ts": 1792082126, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2110771414202744832/vid/avc1/1280x720/KRvaay3M0kus7IMZ.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2110771414202744832/vid/avc1/1920x1080/ENtH22wxd5xxyUhI.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2110771414202744832/img/OjKfZukkVfddNg9Z.jpg", "dur": 99}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 4.86, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}, {"id": "2112310491691601991", "url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2112310491691601991", "text": "Anthropic's @felixrieseberg explains why non-designers love Claude Design, top engineers are less excited about AI coding, and doctors are skeptical of medical AI:\n\n\"People are most excited when AI does something that they can’t do.\"\n\n\"The people most excited about Claude Design are people who do not work full-time in design. I’m super excited about Claude helping me with medical stuff, and my doctor friends are a little more suspicious of that.\"\n\n\"Just because I can take a photograph of the Mona Lisa doesn’t mean the Mona Lisa doesn’t have value anymore. If we talk about these things as if that was that, that’s where the loss of identity comes from.\"\n\n\"I don’t talk to people about this as a coding agent. I talk about it as, this is a means for you to get something done that you couldn’t do before.\"\n@AnthropicAI", "name": "MTS", "handle": "MTSlive", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057947669281263616/aovpVL4b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 27, "rts": 0, "replies": 2, "views": 6034, "ts": 1792449040, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112310457780584448/vid/avc1/640x360/8es5w600Un51HAcW.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112310457780584448/vid/avc1/1280x720/DpHd16ahI8gcHfc4.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112310457780584448/img/3QImUpKrUaDSinhR.jpg", "dur": 115}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 4.82, "thread": [], "tier": "skim"}]);